 "abliterated": {
  "_": "orcarouter's abliterated DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 (orcarouter/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-abliterated: the refusal direction orthogonalized out of every matrix that writes the residual stream - its card: harmful prompts refused 0.874 -> 0.074, MMLU 0.91 -> 0.92) as GGUFs for maya-ds4, two versions (Mix-128G, Mix-256G: the routed experts in other low-bit types layer by layer and role by role, MXFP4 downs under IQ3 gate / ups in some layers; dense weights Q5_K / Q6_K / Q8_0, the router F32), every file at one revision with its size and sha256. Each version's shard 2 holds only the Engram (n-gram) table, IQ4_NL - DeepSeek's released table quantized, not abliterated (checked 2026-10-27: 4096 rows against Maya's Q6_K of it differ as an IQ4_NL quantization of them does, in no shared direction) - so the setup leaves that shard out (\"table\": listed, never fetched) and the pack takes Maya's Q6_K tables instead (\"engram\"), one copy for both versions. Gated on Hugging Face: accept its terms there; the download sends HF_TOKEN (or the token of `hf auth login`). Neither the DSpark drafter nor the vision tower is in it: DeepSeek's (\"drafter\", \"vision\" below), as for unsloth's GGUFs - the drafter only drafts (each token checked by the model), so its answers are the model's own.",
